  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let the function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, be decreasing in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and increasing in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. A tangent to the parabola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;at a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> on it passes through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;but does not pass through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. If the equation of the normal at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "45",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>x</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>But given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>so</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>So function is decreasing in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and increasing&nbsp;in the interval&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now equation of parabola will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></math></p><p>Now tangent to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;will be given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, given this tangent passes through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>,</p><p>So&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>or&#160;</mtext><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>So equation of tangent are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>or&#160;</mtext><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>But&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;passes through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;so rejected as given in the question.</p><p>Now equation of normal at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mtext>as&#160;slope&#160;of&#160;normal&#160;=</mtext><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac><mtext>=-4</mtext></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>32</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>y</mi><mn>36</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
